  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x2BD1" flags="0x0">
    <title>Stationary Limiter Readiness Step</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x13A70; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence candidate. One-dimensional signed-offset step table for stationary rev-limiter readiness accumulator ffff16a6. Every time timer ffff258a expires, FUN 0004f324 decodes the interpolated byte as x-128, adds it to the accumulator with saturation to 0..65535, and reloads the timer with 100. The lookup coordinate is q=clamp((signed16(ffff11bc)-160)/2,0,255). Input ffff11bc is RPM/12.5, so origin 160 is 2000 RPM and each two-count selector step is 25 RPM. At or below 2000 RPM the stock result is 128 and step zero. In the high-RPM limiter region result 255 gives step 127; exactly three expiries reach inclusive readiness threshold 381, or 300 tenth-phase counts. Passive target-CAN timestamps establish 10.24 ms/count and a total of 3.072 seconds. Definition address projected from JK08A 000124d2 through JK08A-JK78C.definition-addresses.csv: unique state-machine accessor preserves the lookup role and geometry.</description>
