  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x2E50" flags="0x0">
    <title>Knock-State Path Enable - Cold State</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x95CA; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence candidate. Cold timing-state surface. Selector 0004e1c0 uses it for both the active sample ffff160f and high-octane reference sample ffff1610 below coolant raw 107, then blends it into both samples through raw 131. The low seven bits feed timing state; bit 7 independently enables a knock-state path. This view edits mask 0x80 and preserves the other bits in each cell. The table is homologous to EV18A 0x9976 with a constant layout offset of +0x5c across the trio. Finisher 000267cc interpolates only bits 0..6 and copies bit 7 from the lower-left selected cell. Code proves relative state flow, but not a direct final angle or physical crank-angle scale. Definition address projected from JK08A 0000991a through JK08A-JK78C.definition-addresses.csv: unique same-contract accessor preserves the 16x16 cold ignition surface role.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="10" />
